      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}: The way audioclips assets are handled in game is depending on their Import settings, they can either be stored in memory compressed and decompressed when playing, or stored in memory uncompressed, or only loaded and uncompressed when an audiosource needs to play it (by default audioclips are set to stored and decompressed on load, so i guess most avatars have those settings)\n\nAnd it will still work this way with the proposed component.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-16T20:53:14.167Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "We really need a feature to allow playing a specific AudioClip on a target AudioSource, using a custom component.\n\nThere are a lot of cases where people wanna play sounds/songs from their avatar, but for each new clips they have to add yet another audiosource to their avatar, even if they don't want to play the clips simultaneously, forcing them to reduce performance for no reason.\n\nThis component would allow people to play lots of differents clips while making sure that only 1 clip can be played simultaneously from that audiosource.\n\nI made an exemple component that is available here:\n\nhttps://github.com/Wakamu/VRC_AvatarAudioPlayer",
